{"term":"sophisticate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:629b84e002f458f167","definition":"To make (something) less innocent or natural; to artificialize.","example":"The party to which Mrs. Berlinton was the loadſtone, was far more attractive to the diſciples of nature, though leſs ſedulouſly ſought by thoſe whom the manners and maxims of the common world had ſophiſticated.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["denaturalize","denature"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6bf64bb29004bf011d","definition":"To make (something) more sophisticated (“complex, developed, or refined”); to develop, to refine.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["complicate","enhance","hone","improve","optimize","perfect","polish"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:77aff1954638ed5ec9","definition":"To make (oneself or someone) more sophisticated (“experienced in the ways of the world, that is, cosmopolitan or worldly-wise”); to cosmopolitanize.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["broaden someone's horizons","deparochialize"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, reflexive","register":"also, reflexive, transitive","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9bdc7b6a1da5a4c689","definition":"To alter and make impure (something) by mixing it with some foreign or inferior substance, especially with an intention to deceive; to adulterate; (generally) to corrupt or deceive (someone, their thinking, etc.).","example":"How be it, it were harde to construe this lecture;\n Sophisticatid craftely is many a confecture; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["abase","bastardize","dash","seduce","subvert","abase","adulter","adulterate","adulterize","alloy","balderdash","corrupt","bastardize","dash","dilute","embase","sophisticate","adulterate","corrupt","debauch","demoralize","detort","file","immoralize","lead astray","pervert","pollute","preposterate","seduce","sophisticate","suborn","subvert","tamper","unmoralize","vitiate","warp"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively","register":"also, figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1d15799ebdab88f08b","definition":"To change the meaning of (something) in a deceptive or misleading way.","example":"The heavy hand of the high Thunderer\n Shall light on thee; and thou I doubt ſhalt be\n His Furies object, and ſhalt teſtifie\n By thine infamous lifes accurſed ſtate,\n VVhat now thy ſhame-leſs lips ſophiſticate.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["distort","pervert","skew","twist"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:81d9f2ba69576f5337","definition":"To apply an artificial technique to (something).","example":"[T]hey ſit in ſome ſun-ſhining place in a chamber or ſome other ſecret roome, where hauing a looking-glaſſe before them they ſophiſticate and dye their haire with the foreſaid drugs, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:865030b433ff4e4ea5","definition":"To practise sophistry (“the (deliberate) making of arguments that seem plausible but are fallacious or misleading”).","example":"The benevolence of her heart taught her, in this inſtance, to ſophiſticate.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2e3c9879776366e24a","definition":"Synonym of sophisticated (adjective).","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f2e5a23748aa0c20eb","definition":"A person who is sophisticated (“experienced in the ways of the world, that is, cosmopolitan or worldly-wise”), or who has sophisticated tastes.","example":"[…] the soporific details of Porter's socially correct marriage of convenience to wealthy and somewhat enigmatic Linda, \"a professional beauty.\" They evidently shared a taste for high social status and the elegant luxuries, high life and freedoms afforded by wealth. Linda and Cole are portrayed as the ultimate sophisticates but the viewer is never told the cause for their separation or why they married.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism","sophisticatedly","sophisticatedness","sophisticating","sophisticative","sophisticator","unsophisticate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sophisticate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/səˈfɪstɪkeɪt/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Qwertygiy-sophisticate.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Qwertygiy-sophisticate.wav.mp3"},"wordFamily":["desophisticate","outsophisticate","sophisticated","sophisticated falsificationism"